  "subject_executed": "ResNet-18 (ImageNet-pretrained) trained on Barcelona PBC 8-class; evaluated on Blood_5 cross-site target (Hao WANG, Zenodo doi:10.5281/zenodo.21628834); 3 seeds, 3 label-alignment scenarios, temperature scaling; genuine cross-site evaluation (different lab, different acquisition)",
  "notes": "Blood_5 from Zenodo 21628834 (doi:10.5281/zenodo.21628834), self-collected by Hao WANG (NOT Barcelona PBC/Acevedo et al.). Downloaded test_batch (5175 images, 150x150x3) via ZIP range-request HTTP (254MB compressed). Key finding: PBC model maps ~95% of Blood5 images to PBC monocyte class, giving 12.8% cross-site accuracy (only true monocytes correct) vs 99.0% in-domain. Severe cross-site overconfidence: ECE=70.3% on Blood5 vs 0.41% in-domain. Source-fit T=1.311 reduces in-domain ECE by 46% (0.41%->0.22%) but only 11% cross-site (70.3%->62.6%): T does NOT repair cross-site miscalibration. CAVEAT: 5x8 confusion matrix row labels in blood5_no_T/with_T are mislabeled (rows index by PBC space 0-7 but labeled with Blood5 class names); 5x5 cm_5x5_C and all accuracy/ECE values are correct."
}